# =============================================================================
# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# The build context is now the WORKSPACE ROOT (it has to be — npm workspaces put
# the lockfile and the hoisted node_modules here, so an app-scoped context could
# not run `npm ci`). That makes this file load-bearing in a way the old
# app-scoped one was not: everything in the repo is a candidate for the context
# now, including the legacy prototypes and the other brand's app.
#
# Keeping this tight makes `docker build` faster (smaller context upload) and
# prevents host-only / secret files from ever entering an image layer.
# The build regenerates node_modules (npm ci) and .next (next build) itself.
# =============================================================================

# Dependencies & build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
out
dist
build

# Version control & CI metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local env / secrets — MUST NOT leak into an image layer.
# (Runtime config is injected at deploy time via AWS Secrets Manager.)
# Note `next build` traces .env into the standalone bundle when it is present,
# so this exclusion is what keeps developer credentials out of the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Terraform state and variable files.
**/infra/terraform/.terraform
**/infra/terraform/*.tfstate
**/infra/terraform/*.tfstate.*
**/infra/terraform/*.tfvars
**/infra/terraform/*.plan
**/infra/terraform/backend.hcl
**/infra/terraform/state-bootstrap/.terraform
**/infra/terraform/state-bootstrap/*.tfstate
**/infra/terraform/state-bootstrap/*.tfstate.*

# Tests, coverage, and TS build cache — not needed to run the app.
**/test
**/tests
**/__tests__
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/vitest.config.ts
**/playwright.config.ts
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# Local SQLite / Prisma dev artifacts (schema + migrations ARE kept).
**/prisma/*.db
**/prisma/*.db-journal

# A developer's local GeoLite2 copy — tens of MB of build context for nothing.
# The build stage downloads its own via scripts/fetch-geoip.mjs.
**/data/geoip/*.mmdb
**/data/geoip/*.partial

# Docs & markdown.
**/*.md
**/docs
*.pdf

# Source media kept in the repo for reference — never needed inside an image.
apps/femi9-web/Testimonial Videos
apps/femi9-web/Femi9_blog images (1)

# Docker files themselves — not needed inside the image.
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore
**/docker-compose.yml
**/docker-compose*.yml

# ── Legacy prototypes at the repo root ───────────────────────────────────────
# Superseded by apps/femi9-web. Dead code, and none of it belongs in an image.
femi9-app
femi9-react
femi9-scrool
femi9-lavender
femi9-scrool.zip
assets
Images
index.html
app.js
styles.css

# ── The other brand ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lumi9 is a separate image. Its SOURCE is excluded, but its package.json is
# re-included: `npm ci` validates the root lockfile against every workspace
# manifest, so an absent manifest fails the install. Excluding the directory's
# *contents* (rather than the directory itself) is what makes the negation work.
apps/lumi9-web/**
!apps/lumi9-web/package.json

# Editor / OS cruft.
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/*.pem
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/*.log
